KZ3 PSO preload (RSX pass 32): record the PSO keys a run uses and pre-create them at the next start.

- Every PSO the walker builds is appended once to <shader cache dir>\pso_keys.bin (key, VS/PS HLSL hash+length =
  the disk cache file names, render state, masked vertex layout, depth bound or not).
- rsx_live_draw_init starts LD_PSO_PRELOAD_THREADS (3) worker threads after the root signature: they read the keys,
  take the bytecode from the shader disk cache files (source + blob, no compile needed) and create the PSOs through
  an ID3D12PipelineLibrary (<dir>\pso_library.bin, serialized on a helper thread when the preload ends, every 60 s
  when it grew and at shutdown; plain creation when ID3D12Device1 or the library is unavailable). Finished PSOs are
  staged and merged into g.psos by the walker before its next lookup and on every present: neither the boot nor the
  walker waits for them.
- The walker's own builds also go through the library (LoadGraphicsPipeline first, StorePipeline after a create).
- apply_render_state takes the depth-bound flag as a parameter (the record keeps it; the key never had it).
- LD_PSO_PRELOAD=0: no workers, no library, recording stays on. LD_PSO_PRELOAD_NOLIB=1: plain creates only.
- [pso-stat] also closes its minute line on every present, and reports "preload used=N".
- Log lines: [pso-preload] start / done (records, library hits, creates, failures, missing blobs, wall ms) /
  library saved / used.
- ppu_crash_report (patch 2030's hunk): the crash file path is logged before the minidump attempt, the result after
  it (the single line after MiniDumpWriteDump never appeared in the round-31 test).

